          %h2#details Details
          %h3#ForFinitelyManyDegreesOfFreedom For finitely many degrees of freedoms
          %p
            We discuss Feynman diagrams for a single real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\in \mathbb{N}
            points. This contains in it already all the aspects of real Feynman diagrams in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            and in this context everything is easily well-defined. The generalization to more field components is immediate and simply obtained by thinking of all “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            ” in the following as taking values in some appropriate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            space and all products of
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiners"} intertwiners
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+products"} inner products
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
          %p
            So a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            here is a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [k]\to \mathbb{R}
            from the
            = succeed "-element" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^k
          %p
            Fix then a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \times k
            real-valued
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Mat
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ×
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \coloneqq (A_{x y}) \in Mat_{k\times k}(\mathbb{R})
            of non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi det
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} det A \neq 0
          %p
            For standard applications this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a discretized version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplacian"} Laplacian
            and then the expression
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi kin
                  %mo ≔
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{kin} = E_{kin} \coloneqq
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x,y = 1}^k \phi_x A_{x y} \phi_y
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+energy"} kinetic energy
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+action"} kinetic action
            of the field configuration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            space points as being a discretization of a circle and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi_p)
            for the corresponding (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+Fourier+transform"}> discrete
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi_x)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            on this space is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+matrix"} diagonal matrix
            in the
            = succeed "-basis" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A_{p,p} = p^2 - m^2
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            is a constant called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            over all values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is the finite (and hence well-defined) analog of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+integral"} Gaussian integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is called the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Z
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi kin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi D
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi k
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %munderover
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi k
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mi π
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi det
                          %mi A
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Z_0
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\int  \exp(- S_{kin}(\phi)) \,D\phi
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\int_{\mathbb{R}^k}
                  \\,
                  \\exp(- \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x,y = 1}^k \phi_{x} A_{x,y} \phi_y  )
                  \\;
                  d\phi_{1} \cdots d\phi_{k}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  (2\pi)^{k/2} (det A)^{-1/2}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            An
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+function"} n-point function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \phi_{x_1} \phi_{x_2} \cdots \phi_{x_n}\rangle
            is an
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moment"} moment
            of this Gaussian distribution:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Z
                                %mn 0
                          %mo ∫
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi kin
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 2
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mi n
                            %mo )
                          %mi D
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Z
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi y
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mn 2
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi x
                                  %mi n
                            %mo )
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\langle \phi_{x_1} \phi_{x_2} \cdots \phi_{x_n}\rangle
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\frac{1}{Z_0}
                  \\int
                  \\left(
                  \\exp(-S_{kin}(\phi))
                  \\phi_{x_1}\phi_{x_2}\cdots \phi_{x_n}
                  \\right)
                  D \phi
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\frac{1}{Z_0}
                  \\int_{\mathbb{R}^k}
                  \\left(
                  \\exp(-\tfrac{1}{2} \phi_x A_{x,y}\phi_y)
                  \\,
                  \\phi_{x_1}\phi_{x_2} \cdots\phi_{x_n}
                  \\right)
                  d\phi_1 \cdots d\phi_k
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            In order to compute these conveniently, pass to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+function"} generating function
            obtained by adding a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = (J_x)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mo ∫
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi kin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi J
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi D
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mi k
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %munderover
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi y
                          %mo +
                          %munderover
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mi d
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi k
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Z
                            %mn 0
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %munderover
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi x
                          %msubsup
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Z(J)
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\int( \exp(- S_{kin}(\phi) + J \cdot\phi) ) D\phi
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\int_{\mathbb{R}^k}
                  \\exp(- \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{x = 1}^k \phi_{x} A_{x,y} \phi_y
                  + \sum_{x = 1}^k J_x \phi_x
                  )
                  \\;
                  d\phi_{1} \cdots d\phi_{k}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  Z_0 \exp(\tfrac{1}{2} \sum_{x = 1}^k J_x A^{-1}_{x,y} J_y)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{-1} = (A^{-1}_{x,y})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+matrix"} inverse matrix
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+integral"} Gaussian integral
            after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completing+the+square"} completing the square
            in the exponent.
          %p
            In applications to field theory this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{-1}
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the kinetic term of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            then in Fourier-transformed components
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{-1}
            is diagonal with components
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A^{-1}_{p,p} = \frac{1}{p^2 - m^2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means, incidentally. that in the non-finite case of interest in physics,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is not actually naively invertible after all, as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2 = m^2
            on the mass
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
