            with its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+regularization"} zeta-function regularized version
          %p
            The way this works is insightful even when the naive
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{-1}
            does exist. Notice that using “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+parameterization"}> Schwinger parameterization
            ” the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagator"} propagator
            is equivalently rewritten as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mellin+transform"} Mellin transform
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi τ
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi d
                  %mi τ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A^{-1}_{p,p} = \int_0^\infty \exp(- \tau A_{p,p}) d\tau
                  \\,.
          %p
            Again in the example of the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            kinetic term expressed in Fourier diagonalization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{p,p}= p^2 - m^2
            then with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon [0,\tau] \to \mathbb{R}
            a parameterization of the straight line with slope
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi τ
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo ,
                              %mi p
                        %mtd
