                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(\phi)
            of degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential+energy"} potential energy
            or (self)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            of the field configuration. The difference of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+energy"} kinetic energy
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential+energy"} potential energy
            is called the (here: “Wick rotated”/“Euclidean”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
