              %p
                This way each sub-graph encodes its corresponding subset of factors in the
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitude"} Feynman amplitude
              %center
                %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FeynmanDiagramComponentTwo.jpg", :width => "560"}/
              %center
                %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FeynmanDiagramComponentThree.jpg", :width => "560"}/
              %blockquote
                %p
                  graphics grabbed from
                  %a{:href => "Feynman+diagram#Brouder10"} Brouder 10
              %p
                A priori this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
                is defined away from coincident vertices:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_0c02e0a3528c2f6e48e15da828bd1c4874be6006_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo ≠
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i \neq x_j
                %math#mathml_0c02e0a3528c2f6e48e15da828bd1c4874be6006_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i = x_j
                requires a choice of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+distributions"} extension of distributions
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
                locus. This choice is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re-")normalization
                of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitude"} Feynman amplitude
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+diagram"} vacuum diagram
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"}> S-matrix
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+series"} perturbation series
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral+quantization"} path integral quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"}> scattering amplitude
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitude"} string scattering amplitude
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline+formalism"} worldline formalism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger-Dyson+equation"} Schwinger-Dyson equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole"} tadpole
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+order"} loop order
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radiative+correction"} radiative correction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"}> graph complex
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formality+of+the+little+n-disk+operad"} formality of the little n-disk operad
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p Traditional review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radovan+Dermisek"}> Radovan Dermisek
                \:
                %em Path integral for interacting field
                (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dermisek-PathIntegralInteractingField.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Weinzierl"}> Stefan Weinzierl
                \:
                %em Introduction to Feynman Integrals
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1005.1855"}> arXiv:1005.1855
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Weinzierl"}> Stefan Weinzierl
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman Integrals
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.03593"} arXiv:2201.03593
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-99558-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-99558-4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Weinzierl"}> Stefan Weinzierl
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman Diagrams
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Particle+Physics"} Encyclopedia of Particle Physics
                (2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.08354"}> arXiv:2501.08354
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"} Matilde Marcolli
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry%2C+Quantum+Fields+and+Motives"} Noncommutative Geometry, Quantum Fields and Motives
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feynman_diagram"} Feynman diagram
            %li
              %p
                F. T. Brandt, J. Frenkel, D. G. C. McKeon,
                %em Feynman diagrams in terms of on-shell propagators
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.14860"}> arXiv:2206.14860
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Zhi-Feng Liu, Yan-Qing Ma,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Determining Feynman Integrals with Only Input from Linear Algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "\nhttps://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.222001\n"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.222001
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11637"} arXiv:2201.11637
          %p
            Discussion via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-modules"} D-modules
          %ul
            %li
              Johannes Henn, Elizabeth Pratt, Anna-Laura Sattelberger, Simone Zoia,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                \-Module Techniques for Solving Differential Equations in the Context of Feynman Integrals
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11105"}> arXiv:2303.11105
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesInCausalPerturbationTheory In causal perturbation theory
          %p
            Discussion of Feynman diagrams in the rigorous formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"} perturbative AQFT
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Keller10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Keller"}> Kai Keller
              , chapter IV of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dimensional Regularization in Position Space and a Forest Formula for Regularized Epstein-Glaser Renormalization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1006.2148"} arXxiv:1006.2148
          %p parts of which also appears as
          %ul
            %li#DuetschFredenhagenKellerRejzner14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Keller"} Kai Keller
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"} Katarzyna Rejzner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dimensional Regularization in Position Space, and a Forest Formula for Epstein-Glaser Renormalization
              %p
                55(12), 122303 (2014) (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.5424"}> arXiv:1311.5424
                )
          %p An exposition of this is in
          %ul
            %li#Brouder10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Brouder"}> Christian Brouder
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multiplication of distributions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BrouderProductOfDistributions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            structure on Feynman diagrams due to
            %a{:href => "renormalization#Kreimer97"} Kreimer 97
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jose+Gracia-Bondia"}> Jose Gracia-Bondia
              , S. Lazzarini,
              %em Connes-Kreimer-Epstein-Glaser Renormalization
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0006106"}> arXiv:hep-th/0006106
              )
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periods"} periods
            (in the sense
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "period#ReferencesInPerturbativeQuantumFieldTheory"} here
          %ul
            %li#Rejzner16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"}> Kasia Rejzner
              ,
              %em Renormalization and periods in perturbative Algebraic Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.02748"}> arXiv:1603.02748
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#HawkinsRejzner16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
              %em The Star Product in Interacting Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.09157"}> arXiv:1612.09157
              )
          %p Review is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"}> Katarzyna Rejzner
              , section 6.5.2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Perturbative Algebraic Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-319-25901-7"} pdf
          %h3#ReferencesInTermsOfMotivicStructures In terms of motivic structures
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives"} motives
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives+in+physics"} motives in physics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spencer+Bloch"}> Spencer Bloch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Helene+Esnault"} Helene Esnault
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirk+Kreimer"} Dirk Kreimer
                %em
                  On motives associated to graph polynomials, (
                  %a{:href => "http://preprints.ihes.fr/2013/P/P-13-24.pdf"}> pdf
                  )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spencer+Bloch"}> Spencer Bloch
                , Pierre Vanhove, The elliptic dilogarithm for the sunset graph, IHES preprint P-13-24, pdf
          %h3#ReferencesInHomologicalBVQuantization In homological BV-quantization
          %p
            A clean derivation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+rules"} Feynman rules
            for finite-dimensional spaces of fields in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            by passing to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-complexes"} BV-complexes
            (see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "geometric%20quantization#AsIndexOfSpinCDiracOperator"}> BV-formalism – Homological quantization
              )
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
              %em How to derive Feynman diagrams for finite-dimensional integrals directly from the BV formalism
              (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.1554"}> arXiv:1202.1554
              )
          %p
            with a review in the broader context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras+of+observables"} factorization algebras of observables
            in section 2.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
              ,
              %em Factorization algebras and free field theories
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GwilliamThesis.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#AsStringDiagrams As string diagrams (morphisms in monoidal categories)
          %p
            It has been observed that Feynman diagrams, notably in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            (in the sense of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            = succeed "!)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/species"} species
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner+classification"} Wigner classification
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreps"} irreps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiners"}> intertwiners
            ”) which, indeed, label the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            of particles in the Feynman diagram.
          %p A review of this formulation is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Lauda"} Aaron Lauda
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Prehistory of n-Categorical Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.2469"} arXiv:0908.2469
          %p
            Moreover, one may think of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            as providing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+nets"} proof nets
            (see there for more) in multiplicative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+nets"} proof nets
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Blute"}> Richard Blute
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prakash+Panangaden"} Prakash Panangaden
              %em Proof nets as formal Feynman diagrams
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.indiana.edu/~iulg/qliqc/phi.pdf"}> pdf
              )
        .revisedby
